WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.520
<v Nicolas Palma>Here with us are two plastic surgeons, big names in plastic surgery,

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:08.880
<v Nicolas Palma>clients of ours at the agency, and they're going to talk a bit about what the experience has been like here at MedGrowth.

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:09.780
<v Nicolas Palma>So, Doc?

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:15.100
<v Dr. Ícaro Samuel>Guys, here's the thing: MedGrowth is here to help us improve our paid traffic,

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:19.640
<v Dr. Ícaro Samuel>it's here to make it happen, to turn the lead into a consultation,

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:22.460
<v Dr. Ícaro Samuel>to help us grow and leverage our clinic.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:30.220
<v Dr. Ícaro Samuel>And they definitely have the best opportunity to help the surgeon understand the process,

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:34.060
<v Dr. Ícaro Samuel>because this is hard. We surgeons don't really understand what paid traffic is.

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:37.640
<v Dr. Ícaro Samuel>We don't understand that traffic also depends on the creative.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:42.640
<v Dr. Ícaro Samuel>Many surgeons don't know what a creative is. And the creative depends on you making a video.

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:48.560
<v Dr. Ícaro Samuel>Then they blame the traffic for not bringing the right lead, and your sales team isn't trained.

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:52.400
<v Dr. Ícaro Samuel>So it's a series of factors that they manage to make clearer, more didactic.

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:58.940
<v Dr. Ícaro Samuel>We start understanding the process, and it helps our clinic grow, as a result, with the tool they provide.

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:02.080
<v Dr. Ícaro Samuel>And that's a win-win; everyone's in it together.

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:03.820
<v Dr. Rafael Sabino>Hard to add anything, you know?

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:07.060
<v Dr. Rafael Sabino>But without a doubt, it's an incredible company, incredible guys.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:13.100
<v Dr. Rafael Sabino>It stops being that company we picture as a bunch of people you don't know, doing the same work for everyone.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:15.580
<v Dr. Rafael Sabino>No, it's very personalized. I think that's the company's big differentiator.

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:20.540
<v Dr. Ícaro Samuel>Personalization. Because in plastic surgery especially, there's no point in being

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:23.520
<v Dr. Ícaro Samuel>the same for everyone. It has to be personalized.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:27.760
<v Dr. Ícaro Samuel>And that's why, in the short time I've been with them, there has already been great progress,

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:30.600
<v Dr. Ícaro Samuel>precisely because each person has their own characteristics.

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:33.920
<v Dr. Ícaro Samuel>There's no point copying Rafael. There's no point copying Ícaro.

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:37.760
<v Dr. Ícaro Samuel>It's personalized, and they help: "your style is this, your style is that,

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:39.660
<v Dr. Ícaro Samuel>let's do it this way, the creative."

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:43.440
<v Dr. Ícaro Samuel>And as a result, we gain from it. Gain what?

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:50.220
<v Dr. Ícaro Samuel>Bringing in leads; the lead turns into a client for the consultation, and the consultation turns into surgery. That's our goal.
